{"task_id": "HumanEval/39", "solution": "def prime_fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_fib returns n-th number that is a Fibonacci number and it's also prime.\n    >>> prime_fib(1)\n    2\n    >>> prime_fib(2)\n    3\n    >>> prime_fib(3)\n    5\n    >>> prime_fib(4)\n    13\n    >>> prime_fib(5)\n    89\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to check if a number is prime.\n    def is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        if num <= 1:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    # Initialize Fibonacci sequence variables and a counter for prime Fibonacci numbers.\n    fib_a, fib_b = 0, 1\n    count = 0\n\n    # Generate Fibonacci numbers until the n-th prime Fibonacci number is found.\n    while True:\n        next_fib = fib_a + fib_b\n        \n        # Update Fibonacci sequence for the next iteration.\n        fib_a = fib_b\n        fib_b = next_fib\n\n        # Check if the generated Fibonacci number is prime and greater than 1.\n        if next_fib > 1 and is_prime(next_fib):\n            count += 1\n            if count == n:\n                return next_fib"}
